Does Nethack3.0 (or 2.3) support multiple systems sharing 1 save directory ?

We have a group of Suns which access our current version of Nethack (2.2 or 2.3)
over NFS.  They all use the same save directory, so if more than one person
is playing, and not all of the people are on the same host, the level lock files
get messed up, causing most games to die.  What would be nice is for the UNIX
version of nethack to append a host name or something to make a file unique
across users and hosts.

If 3.0 doesn't have this feature, I may try and do it for our version.
Does anyone else think this is a worth while addition ?

